  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected relationship between 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and SW948, with multiple pathways converging on the target SW948 through different intermediates. The compound directly targets Leukocyte common antigen, which in turn is a target of Mollicellin N, and both are linked to SW948. Additionally, the compound also targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4C, which is a target of another compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which also targets SW948. These findings indicate that 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid may exert its effects through multiple molecular mechanisms, potentially influencing SW948 via different pathways. The integration of these targets suggests a broader role for the compound in modulating cellular processes associated with SW948, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
